Z||000000||William||02-18-2001||11:25 PM||||I just read a post on the Fiero email list regarding Fiero carpet. The post states that all 84-87 Fieros had the pad separate from the carpet with only the 88's having the molded on rubber pad? MrMike's site infers that all fiero carpeting has the molded on padding. Can anyone who has ripped out there carpeting confirm who's correct? This will effect how I lay down the new carpeting. Thx!!!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula 18||02-18-2001||11:44 PM||||I can tell you that in my 88 formula there is a spongy molded sounds dampener molded right in with the carpet. It actually lokks gluded on there b/c it is not the same material and the rubber backing. It all came out as on piece though. <P>Hope this helps. <BR>Brian ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||02-18-2001||11:50 PM||||My 86 has the rubber-molded carpet. I cut carpet out of an 85 for my subwoofer project and it had rubber backing. I'm inclined to think the author of the post on the mailing list thinks he has Lotus suspension, too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||02-19-2001||01:27 AM||||I've never really noticed to tell you the truth but there are two kinds - one with the molded in rubber and one with separate glued on fiber fill pads (I just replaced a complete beechwood interior on an '88 with gray, the carpet I removed ('88) was molded rubber - the carpet I replaced it with (came out of an '87) was the fiber fill pad.......||||reg||1
